"""Original data-model, import and access-control cases."""
ITEMS=[]
def group(o,rows):
 for k,(s,e) in enumerate(rows):ITEMS.append((s,[o[k]]+[v for j,v in enumerate(o) if j!=k],e))
group(['Create a separate table','Add a field to the table','Create a new record','Use a reference to another table'],[
('A new application needs a distinct collection of equipment-inspection records with its own defined fields. Which schema action provides the collection?', 'A table defines the collection and its fields. An individual record is one entry within it.'),
('Every inspection record needs a new numeric measurement in addition to its existing attributes. Which schema change adds that attribute?', 'Add a suitable field to the existing table rather than create an unrelated record to represent the column.'),
('The inspection schema is already correct. A technician now needs to enter the results of one additional inspection. Which data action fits?', 'Create a new record using the existing schema; no new table or field is required for each inspection.'),
('An inspection should identify an existing technician from the user table while maintaining a relationship to that user record. Which field design fits?', 'A reference relates the inspection to the existing user record rather than duplicating all user attributes as independent text.')])
group(['An integer field','A date/time field','A reference field','A true/false field'],[
('A custom record needs to store the whole-number count of inspected devices, with numeric comparison and calculation. Which field type fits?', 'An integer represents whole-number quantities rather than a text description or record reference.'),
('A record must capture the scheduled moment of a maintenance visit, including both calendar date and time. Which field type fits?', 'A date/time field represents the required temporal value.'),
('A request must point to one existing department record and allow use of that record’s other attributes. Which field type fits?', 'A reference field links to the department record and supports related-field access.'),
('A record needs a binary indicator of whether a checklist is complete. Which field type fits?', 'A true/false field represents the two-state value directly.')])
group(['Inspect the dictionary definition','Inspect the dictionary override','Inspect the schema relationship','Inspect the stored record value'],[
('A field has the wrong underlying data type across the relevant table. Which metadata should be examined rather than only rearranging the form?', 'The dictionary describes the field’s underlying definition. Form layout does not change its data type.'),
('An inherited field behaves differently on one child table because a child-specific definition has been configured. Which metadata should be examined?', 'A dictionary override can define supported field behavior differently on an extended table.'),
('An administrator needs to determine which table extends which other table before changing a shared field. Which structural information is relevant?', 'Inspect the table hierarchy or schema relationship to understand inheritance and affected classes.'),
('Only one record contains an incorrect department reference, while the field definition and other records are correct. Which object needs investigation?', 'Inspect the record’s stored value rather than changing the schema for every record.')])
group(['The reference’s stored sys_id','The referenced record’s display value','The reference qualifier','A dot-walked related field'],[
('Two user records have the same displayed name. An administrator needs to distinguish which actual record a reference points to. Which value is decisive?', 'The stored sys_id identifies the referenced record even when display names are identical.'),
('A reference appears as a readable person name on a form instead of a long identifier. Which value is being presented?', 'The UI presents the referenced record’s display value while the reference stores its identifier.'),
('A reference picker offers inactive departments that should not be selectable in this UI. Which field configuration should narrow the offered choices?', 'A reference qualifier filters the candidates offered by the picker; access controls remain separate.'),
('A report needs the city on the location record referenced by a task. Which field access supplies that related attribute?', 'Dot-walking follows the reference to the related location’s city rather than requiring a copied field on every task.')])
group(['Assign the approved role to a group','Add the user to the approved group','Remove the obsolete group membership','Review all effective role sources'],[
('Every member of an established support group needs the same approved platform capability. Which administration action avoids assigning the role separately to each person?', 'Assign the approved role to the group so members inherit it.'),
('A new employee needs the access already granted through the authorized team group. The group’s roles are correct. Which lifecycle action fits?', 'Add the employee to the approved group rather than redefining its existing roles.'),
('An employee leaves a team and should no longer inherit that team’s permissions. No continuing need is approved. Which source of access should be removed?', 'Remove the obsolete group membership and verify remaining access according to the lifecycle process.'),
('Removing one group membership does not remove a user’s capability. The same role may come from another group or a direct grant. What should be examined?', 'Review every effective source of the role before assuming the membership change failed.')])
group(['The read operation','The write operation','The create operation','The delete operation'],[
('A security requirement concerns whether a user may view an existing confidential record. Which ACL operation is directly relevant?', 'Read governs viewing the protected object; other operations address different actions.'),
('A user may see a record but must not modify its existing values. Which ACL operation governs the attempted modification?', 'Write governs modification. Read permission does not itself imply write permission.'),
('A policy concerns whether a user may add a new record to a protected table. Which ACL operation is directly relevant?', 'Create governs adding a record, distinct from modifying an existing one.'),
('A user may maintain a record but must not remove it from the table. Which ACL operation governs removal?', 'Delete governs removing the protected record.')])
group(['Review the required role alternatives','Review the data condition','Review the permission script result','Review the ACL decision type'],[
('A non-admin user satisfies one of two roles listed in an ACL’s Requires role list. A reviewer incorrectly assumes both listed roles are necessary. Which part of the rule should be re-examined?', 'The listed roles are alternatives for that role check. Other applicable conditions still need evaluation.'),
('A user passes an ACL’s role requirement, but the rule requires a department value that the requested record does not have. Which part explains the failed check?', 'The data condition is separate from the role requirement and must satisfy the configured policy.'),
('An applicable ACL has satisfied role and data conditions, but its custom permission code evaluates to false. Which part explains that rule’s failure?', 'The permission script must evaluate successfully as required by the ACL; passing the other checks does not override a false script result.'),
('An administrator is reviewing a current ACL configured as Deny Unless and must distinguish it from an Allow If rule. Which property determines that behavior?', 'Decision Type distinguishes the current supported ACL decision behavior. A blanket assumption that every ACL is an Allow If rule is incorrect.')])
group(['Inspect the staged source rows','Correct the field mapping','Configure the coalesce key','Review the transformation result'],[
('An import loaded a spreadsheet, but some source dates are already malformed before any target records are changed. Where should the administrator first inspect the imported values?', 'Inspect the staged source rows to distinguish source/load problems from later mapping or target behavior.'),
('A test import places a source phone number into the target city field. Which transformation configuration directly needs correction?', 'Correct the source-to-target field mapping. A coalesce key selects a matching record but does not fix mapping to the wrong field.'),
('A recurring import should update the existing equipment record identified by a stable external identifier instead of adding another copy. Which matching configuration is needed?', 'Coalesce on a suitable stable identifier to match the intended existing target record, subject to verified uniqueness and import requirements.'),
('A transformation has finished, but the administrator needs evidence of inserted, updated and failed rows before accepting the load. Which review is required?', 'Review the transformation outcome and affected target data rather than treating completion alone as proof of correct results.')])
group(['One update and one insert','Two updates and no inserts','No updates and two inserts','One update and no inserts'],[
('A target table has unique external keys A and B. A two-row import contains keys A and C and coalesces only on that key. No rows are rejected and normal unmatched-row insertion is enabled. What is the result?', 'A matches an existing record and is updated; C does not match and is inserted.'),
('A target table has unique asset keys D and E. An import contains one changed row for D and one for E, with valid values and matching coalesce configuration. What is the result?', 'Both source rows match existing records, so both are updates and neither is an insert.'),
('Two valid rows are transformed into a table with no coalesce fields configured. No custom script changes normal behavior. What is the result?', 'Without coalesce, the two imported rows are treated as new records rather than matching existing records for updates.'),
('A valid single source row uses external key F, and exactly one target record has F. Coalesce is configured on that key. What is the result?', 'The one matching target record is updated; there is no unmatched row to insert.')])
group(['Maintain the configuration item record','Maintain the CI relationship','Follow the CSDM placement guidance','Correct the incoming data mapping'],[
('The CMDB has the right server record, but its operating-system attribute is inaccurate. Which data-maintenance action directly addresses this?', 'Correct the relevant CI record attribute using the appropriate authoritative process.'),
('The CMDB contains both an application and its supporting database, but the dependency between them is missing. Which modeling element needs attention?', 'Maintain the relationship between the CIs so dependency and impact analysis can use it.'),
('Teams place equivalent service information into inconsistent tables and use conflicting terminology. Which shared modeling guidance should guide reconciliation?', 'CSDM provides common terminology and guidance for placing service-related information in the appropriate CMDB structures.'),
('A third-party feed sends valid source data, but the integration places it into the wrong CMDB fields. Which integration detail needs correction?', 'Correct the data mapping and validate the transformed output; creating more relationships does not repair a field-mapping error.')])
group(['Review the instance’s security settings','Review customer data-retention decisions','Review platform infrastructure protection','Review the custom application’s security'],[
('An organization has granted an overly broad role within its ServiceNow instance. Which customer-controlled security area must be corrected?', 'The customer controls its instance authorization and secure configuration; provider infrastructure controls do not choose appropriate business access.'),
('A business has never decided how long its customer records should remain in the instance. Which responsibility needs an explicit policy decision?', 'The customer defines appropriate data use and retention obligations rather than assuming a provider default satisfies every requirement.'),
('An assurance review asks how the hosted platform’s underlying infrastructure is secured by ServiceNow. Which responsibility area should be examined?', 'ServiceNow protects the platform infrastructure as part of its provider responsibilities, distinct from customer entitlement decisions.'),
('A customer-developed application has an authorization flaw in its own logic. Which security responsibility must the customer exercise?', 'The customer is responsible for the security of its custom code and its appropriate development and validation process.')])
group(['Review best-practice adoption','Review privileged-account posture','Review unused-account posture','Review assigned security tasks'],[
('A security administrator wants to see how many recommended instance practices have been applied and how that count changed over time. Which Security Center view focus fits?', 'The best-practice area tracks adoption and progress, distinct from individual account or task lists.'),
('A review focuses on active accounts with elevated permissions in the instance. Which posture information is directly relevant?', 'Privileged-account posture helps identify the population with elevated access for review.'),
('An administrator wants to investigate enabled users that have never signed in. Which posture information supports that review?', 'Unused-account posture identifies the relevant never-logged-in population; it does not itself determine whether every such account should be removed.'),
('A security operator needs the urgent remediation work allocated to them. Which Security Center area directly supports that work list?', 'Assigned security tasks identify the operator’s work, rather than only showing summary posture counts.')])
ops=['Read existing records','Modify existing records','Create new records','Delete existing records']
for s,k,e in [
('A reviewer must inspect existing records and correct approved values, but must neither add nor remove records. Choose the two operations the requirement allows.',[0,1],'The requirement permits read and write, while explicitly excluding create and delete.'),
('A service identity may create new records and modify existing records. Viewing records is handled separately and deletion is forbidden. Choose the two operations explicitly authorized here.',[1,2],'Create and write are the two stated authorizations. Do not infer other permissions from them.'),
('A controlled cleanup process is explicitly authorized to add replacement records and remove obsolete records. Modification and reading are outside this question’s authorization. Choose the two stated operations.',[2,3],'Create and delete are explicitly authorized; the question does not grant additional operations.'),
('An archive reviewer may inspect existing records and remove records approved for disposal, but may not create or edit records. Choose the two allowed operations.',[3,0],'Read and delete match the stated policy; write and create are excluded.')]:ITEMS.append((s,ops,e,k))
checks=['Validate the matching key','Test the field mappings','Restrict staging-data access','Verify the target results']
for s,k,e in [
('Before an import, the team must prove that the chosen external identifier uniquely selects the intended records and that each source column reaches the correct target field. Choose the two checks addressing those stated gaps.',[0,1],'Validate the matching key and test mappings. The other checks remain useful controls but do not establish these two specific properties.'),
('An import trial sends values into the wrong target fields, and sensitive staged rows are readable by an unintended group. Choose the two checks that address these observed problems.',[1,2],'Test and correct mappings, and restrict staging access. Key validation alone does not fix either observed issue.'),
('A completed import has not been checked against expected target records, and the staging table contains personal data with unreviewed access. Choose the two checks needed for these stated gaps.',[2,3],'Review staging access and verify the target outcome. Neither step is replaced by a successful load status.'),
('A recurring import created duplicate target records and the final target population has not been reconciled. Source-to-field mappings and staging access are already verified. Choose the two remaining checks.',[3,0],'Validate the matching key and reconcile target results. The stated evidence rules out the other two checks as the remaining gaps.')]:ITEMS.append((s,checks,e,k))
assert len(ITEMS)==56
